## The power the ADCS's sensors draw in a flight mode (S11.8, Y1; decision DR-design-003: the scope of the power budget is the
## whole ADCS). A fitted sensor draws its steady power (the part's power_steady_W, else its power_W, the units of the fill
## line counted as the budget counts them: sizebudget's budget_line) for as long as the ADCS is powered, except the star
## tracker, which the flight software's modes do not use while the body is detumbling, spinning or acquiring the Sun (the
## tracker is blind above its rate limit and the modes hold the attitude by the Sun, the field and the gyro) and which is
## then off; it is on in the modes that estimate an attitude from it (nadir, target, slew and fine Sun pointing). The rule is
## the developer's, unsigned: each sensor's duty by mode is a stated choice for the owner to sign or replace.
## The flight modes are those of the flight software's table (ADCS_MODE_*): 0 detumble, 1 nadir by coils, 2 nadir fine,
## 3 target fine, 4 slew fine, 5 spin-up, 6 Sun spin, 7 detumble by thrusters, 8 Sun acquisition by rotors, 9 Sun by coils,
## 10 Sun fine; a mode not in the table (255, no mode yet) is taken as one that powers every sensor but the tracker.
## Powers in W: plain numbers.
## The developer's revision (S11.8), unsigned.
module sensorpower

## The ADCS's sensors, in the order sensor_power takes their powers: the gyro, the magnetometer, the fine Sun sensors, the
## coarse Sun sensors, the star tracker, the Earth sensor and the GNSS receiver.
choice Sensor = gyro, magnetometer, sun_sensors, coarse_sun_sensors, star_tracker, earth_sensor, gnss

## Whether sensor s is powered in flight mode `mode`.
fn sensor_on(mode: int in 0 .. 255, s: Sensor) -> on: bool
    on = true
    if s == Sensor.star_tracker
        on = (mode >= 1 and mode <= 4) or mode == 10
    end
end

## The power of the sensors in flight mode `mode` [W], from each sensor's whole steady power p (every unit of the fill
## line, in the order of Sensor: 0 where the product fits none), summed from zero in that order.
fn sensor_power(mode: int in 0 .. 255, p: real[1][7] in 0 .. 5) -> total: real[1]
    total = 0.0
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.gyro)
        total = total + p[0]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.magnetometer)
        total = total + p[1]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.sun_sensors)
        total = total + p[2]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.coarse_sun_sensors)
        total = total + p[3]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.star_tracker)
        total = total + p[4]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.earth_sensor)
        total = total + p[5]
    end
    if sensor_on(mode, Sensor.gnss)
        total = total + p[6]
    end
end
